--- !u!1001 &2127602961
PrefabInstance:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  serializedVersion: 2
  m_Modification:
    serializedVersion: 3
    m_TransformParent: {fileID: 1936824525}
    m_Modifications:
    - target: {fileID: 3657750595127706157, guid: 83f67faf358644b34ad60e68c9dc8f56, type: 3}
      propertyPath: dialogueObjects.Array.size
      value: 6
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3657750595127706157, guid: 83f67faf358644b34ad60e68c9dc8f56, type: 3}
      propertyPath: dialogueObjects.Array.data[0]._dialogueText
      value: <NAME>, did you know that polynomials have different names depending
        on the highest degree?
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3657750595127706157, guid: 83f67faf358644b34ad60e68c9dc8f56, type: 3}
      propertyPath: dialogueObjects.Array.data[1]._dialogueText
      value: A polynomial to the 2nd degree is referred to as a quadratic polynomial.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3657750595127706157, guid: 83f67faf358644b34ad60e68c9dc8f56, type: 3}
      propertyPath: dialogueObjects.Array.data[2]._dialogueText
      value: A polynomial to the 3rd degree is known to as a cubic polynomial.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3657750595127706157, guid: 83f67faf358644b34ad60e68c9dc8f56, type: 3}
      propertyPath: dialogueObjects.Array.data[3]._dialogueText
      value: Additionally, a polynomial to the 4th degree is known to as a quartic
        polynomial.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3657750595127706157, guid: 83f67faf358644b34ad60e68c9dc8f56, type: 3}
      propertyPath: dialogueObjects.Array.data[4]._dialogueText
      value: You can keep going higher with them, but it is crucial to identify these
        three!
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3657750595127706157, guid: 83f67faf358644b34ad60e68c9dc8f56, type: 3}
      propertyPath: dialogueObjects.Array.data[5]._dialogueText
      value: Higher degrees exist, but won't be relevant for your adventure!
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 7782682502209912324, guid: 83f67faf358644b34ad60e68c9dc8f56, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_LocalPosition.x
      value: 109
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
